Subject: [PATCH v5 9/9] jails/instances/lab-mail: Take posts for the
 lists.p7x.dev lists
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: mxytnonnzulosvkynknsvqvvotnplwmv
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:01:22 +0000

The hub should carry lab@lists.p7x.dev and freebsd-ports@lists.p7x.dev
as well as lab-devel@p7x.dev. Mail to either of those addresses would
otherwise be refused at RCPT TO, so the client would drop the message
and it would reach no one.

- smtpd.conf's table list names all three addresses.
- The spec and README.org name them, and say that the Fastmail rule
  must file all three into lists.
- A message to two list addresses lands once for each, since
  OpenSMTPD delivers each recipient separately. The spec says so,
  and that notmuch still shows it once.
